[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should be set up from the start?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests, node --test (recommended)
  [38;5;246mNode's built-in runner. Zero dependencies, native ES modules. Covers store.js and storage.js logic.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Linting + formatting
  [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier as devDependencies. Adds a node_modules to an otherwise dependency-free project.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] E2E tests (Playwright)
  [38;5;246mReal browser tests for the UI flows. Genuinely useful, but a heavy dependency for an app this size.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — just build it
  [38;5;246mNo test or lint infrastructure. Fastest to working code, but sub-project 2 lands on an untested base.[39m
